James sought a method to "fade" colors in ggplot without using transparency. I suggested using the `lighten()` function from the `colorspace` package to achieve a "whitened" effect. I recommended first installing the `colorspace` package, followed by defining an original color and applying `lighten()` to modify it towards white. I provided a code snippet demonstrating how to achieve this effect within a `ggplot` context. The `amount` parameter in `lighten()` allows for controlled whitening, with values ranging from 0 (no change) to 1 (full whitening).
